whip_bridge is an independent implementation. It is not affiliated with,
endorsed by, or sponsored by any of the projects it bridges to.

The projects it targets, and their licenses:

  qb-core, qb-inventory, qb-target, qb-menu, qb-input, qb-vehiclekeys
    QBCore Framework, GPL-3.0
  qbx_core, qbx_vehiclekeys
    Qbox Project, GPL-3.0
  ox_inventory, ox_target
    Overextended, LGPL-3.0

whip_bridge targets the public interface of those resources: the export names,
event names and data shapes that a script written for them expects. It contains
no code from them.

The name "qbx_core" appears here as a provided resource name, as a prefix on
event names, and as the compatibility shim in compat/. In each case it names the
Qbox resource that third-party scripts expect to call, not this project.
